note seed/node/release.om -- omnode-release, the Omega Node release lifecycle (DRA-292):
note build, serve, start, health, stop, restore, unserve, snapshot and rollback of one
note coding workflow. OM-2 program; compose after om/tls/sha2.om (SHA-256):
note   { printf 'om2\n'; cat om/tls/sha2.om seed/node/release.om; } | seed/out/omc > build/node/release
note Every program it starts is compiled from .om (the six of build, and omc) except the
note own-model server OLLM, which serve starts as given. Children get an empty environment
note (execprog), descriptors 0..2 only, and no PATH search.
note   release build OUT
note       Compose and compile infer, tool, code-main, code-test, op and fake-serve into OUT with
note       seed/out/omc; one BUILD_OK name bytes sha256 (or BUILD_FAIL name message) line each,
note       then omc sha256. Run from the checkout root: the units and omc are found there.
note   release serve STATE PORT OLLM VERB CK MERGES
note       Start OLLM VERB PORT CK MERGES; STATE/serve.pid, serve.log; wait for its PORT line.
note   release start STATE BIN OMC PORT VIEW
note       Write STATE/release.env and start code-main on STATE (root/, work/, journal/,
note       objs.txt: one objective per line); node.pid; append run.out and run.err; wait until
note       the view answers. Refuses (exit 3) while node.pid is alive.
note   release health STATE     the model's GET /health and the view; 0 when both answer
note   release stop STATE       pause (op 1), wait until nothing runs or is in review (900 s),
note                            SIGTERM; view-at-stop.json
note   release restore STATE    start again on the same journal, resume (op 2) when paused
note   release unserve STATE    SIGTERM the model server
note   release snapshot STATE SNAP   copy STATE/root, work, journal into SNAP (new)
note   release rollback STATE SNAP   replace STATE/root, work, journal with SNAP's copies
note Errors: one line "release: MESSAGE" on stderr; exit 2 usage or never 18091, 3 a process
note in the wrong state, 1 any other failure.

text rlpre "release: "
text rlnl "\n"
text rlsp " "
text rlnull "/dev/null"
